{"headword":"מָצוֹר⁴","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>siege-enclosure, siege, entrenchment;</strong>—always <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> abs., exc. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְצוֹר</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.7\">Ez 4:7</a>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְצוּרֶ֑ךָ</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.8\">8</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>siege</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ שָׂם עָלֵינוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 4:14\" href=\"/Micah.4.14\">Mi 4:14</a> <em>he hath laid siege to us</em>, cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְנָתַתָּ֫ עָלֶיהָ מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.2\">Ez 4:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בּוֹא בַמּ׳</span> is <em>come into a state of siege</em> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 20:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.20.19\">Dt 20:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 24:10\" href=\"/II_Kings.24.10\">2 K 24:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 25:2\" href=\"/II_Kings.25.2\">25:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 52:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.52.5\">Je 52:5</a>, cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְהָֽיְתָה בַמּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.3\">Ez 4:3</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">יוֹשֶׁבֶת֯י בַּמּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 10:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.10.17\">Je 10:17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מְצוֹר יְרו׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.7\">Ez 4:7</a> <em>siege of</em> Jerus., but also <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ עַל־יְרו׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 12:2\" href=\"/Zechariah.12.2\">Zc 12:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">יְמֵי מ׳</span> of duration of siege <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 4:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.4.8\">Ez 4:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.2\">5:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵי מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:14\" href=\"/Nahum.3.14\">Na 3:14</a> <em>water for a siege;</em> in phr. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּמ׳ וּבְמָצוֹק</span> <em>in the siege and stress</em> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:53\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.53\">Dt 28:53</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:55\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.55\">55</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:57\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.57\">57</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 19:9\" href=\"/Jeremiah.19.9\">Je 19:9</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>enclosure</em>, i.e. <em>siege-works</em> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 20:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.20.20\">Dt 20:20</a>; late = <em>rampart</em> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:3\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.3\">Zc 9:3</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">עִיר מ׳</span> <em>entrenched city</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 31:22\" href=\"/Psalms.31.22\">ψ 31:22</a> (al. <em>besieged</em>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 60:11\" href=\"/Psalms.60.11\">60:11</a> (‖ <a data-ref=\"Psalms 108:11\" href=\"/Psalms.108.11\">108:11</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳מִבְצָר</span>), cf. <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 8:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.8.5\">2 Ch 8:5</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עָרִים לְמ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 11:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.11.5\">11:5</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ישְׁבִים בְּמ׳ בִּירוּשָׁלַם</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 32:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.32.10\">32:10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 2:1\" href=\"/Habakkuk.2.1\">Hb 2:1</a> according to most (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מִשְׁמֶרֶת</span>); but We der. from <span dir=\"rtl\">נצר</span>, i.e. <em>watch</em>-tower, Now conj. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִצְפֶּה</span> (cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, מִצְפֶּה\" href=\"/BDB,_מִצְפֶּה\", dir=\"rtl\">וַאֲצַפֶּה</a> foll.); > Buhl conj. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְצָד—מ׳</span> <strong>n.pr.terr.</strong> v. p. 596."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDB08326","strong_numbers":["4686","4692","4693"],"next_hw":"מְצוּרָה","prev_hw":"צוּר","all_cited":true,"ordinal":"I.","quotes":[],"GK":["5189","5190","5191","5192"],"TWOT":["1885g","1898a"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and 